    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d341">

                <pb facs="0664" n="604" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg604"/>

                <head>Mr. La Reintrie to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 99.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Consulate General of the United
                                States</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Havana</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-10-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 6, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: At the request of Mr. Romero I transmit you
                        the<anchor n="*" xml:id="d341-f1"/> Diario Oficial of Mexico, of the 24th
                    ultimo. It contains the documents showing the latest attempted <hi
                        rendition="#italic">coup d’état</hi> of Santa Anna for upsetting the
                    government of President Juarez. As the steamer leaves in a few minutes, I have
                    not the time to have it translated. The attempt has completely failed, as will
                    also any other on the part of Santa Anna. I am, sir, with great respect, your
                    obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. R. DE LA BEINTRIE, <hi rendition="#italic">Vice-Consul
                        General.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d341-f1" n="*" xml:id="d341-f1-content">
                <p>For inclosure see inclosure to Mr. Plumb’s dispatch, No. 193, of the 25th
                    September.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
